course: dictionary
lesson: 5383
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are the context. «She turned the knob and the door swung open.» A knob here is a round handle you turn to open a door, because that is what you turn to open a door.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «Turn the volume knob to make the music quieter.» This knob is a round button you turn to control a machine. The clue is what you are turning: a door in one sentence, a sound machine in the other.
explain: Some knobs are not handles or buttons at all. «A knob of butter» is a small lump of butter, and «a knob on a tree trunk» is a small round lump. Try each meaning in the sentence, and keep the one that still makes sense.
fact: Knob (noun) can mean a round handle, a round button you turn, a small round lump, or a small lump of something soft like butter.
fact: «Door knob» means the round handle you turn to open a door.
fact: «Volume knob» means the round button you turn to make a radio louder or quieter.
fact: «A knob of butter» means a small lump of butter, used in cooking.
fact: A gas cooker knob controls the gas and the heat. If a flame goes out while the gas is on, turn the knob off and tell a grown-up.
exercise: «She turned the knob and the door swung open.» What is a knob here? | A loud noise | A round lump on a tree trunk | A small cake | *A round handle you turn to open a door
exercise: «Add a knob of butter to the pan.» What does knob mean here? | A bright light | *A small lump of butter | A tiny round handle | A long wooden stick
exercise: «Turn the volume knob to make the music quieter.» What does the knob do? | A bright light | A lock that keeps a door shut | *A round button you turn to control a machine | A sort of cake
test: «The cook turned the knob to lower the heat.» What does knob mean here? | A bump on a bone | A door handle | *A round button you turn to control the heat | A small round lump
test: «The microscope has a focus knob.» What does the focus knob do? | A kind of door | *A round button you turn to sharpen the picture | A glass that holds water | A lamp that shines in the dark
exam: «Turn the knob off and tell a grown-up.» Which thing is most likely to have a knob here? | A soft toy | *A gas cooker | A library book | A bicycle bell
